      Enable Bypass permissions?
      Elpis will run anything without asking: any command, any file on
      this computer, the internet. It also runs commands it would
      otherwise refuse, such as rm -rf, and in new sessions it runs
      enabled hooks you have not reviewed.

      Only your own rules, hooks and managed policy can still stop it. Use
      it only where you would give Elpis root access.


    › 1. Cancel                   Go back without bypassing permissions
      2. Yes, bypass permissions  Run anything without asking in this
                                  session

      enter select · esc back
